      part: { q: 'What\'s the plug telling you?', a: ['Healthy plug', 'Plug ran HOTTER than design — wrong heat range, ignition timing too advanced, or pre-ignition', 'Normal wear', 'Worn from age only: the white insulator and rounded electrode are what a plug looks like after 60,000 miles'], correct: 1 },
      cause: { q: 'Likely root cause?', a: ['Bad fuel only', 'Lean fuel mixture (not enough fuel) OR knock-controller failure OR vacuum leak on this cylinder', 'Defective plug from the factory, with an insulator that cracked and let heat build up inside the shell', 'Cold weather'], correct: 1 },
